{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Balaam refused to go with us.</b> They suspected him of being a liar and attributed the matter to him — that his eyes were not satisfied with this measure of honor. Or perhaps, because he had told them that he would give them an answer immediately, as soon as HaShem would speak to him at night, yet he did not do so until morning, they said: this is nothing other than his own words. Or it is possible that he was well established as one whose mouth speaks falsehood and whose right hand is a right hand of vanity, etc."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:12:28.153345273Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}